===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|obsolete}} To [[deliver]], especially in context of [[sin]] or relevant penalties. {{defdate|14th century}}
# To pay a price to set someone free from [[captivity]] or [[punishment]].
#: {{usex|en|to '''ransom''' prisoners from an enemy}}
#* {{RQ:Marlowe Tamburlaine|part=1|scene=ii|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=0HFGOmnsvAMC&pg=PP25|passage=And gainſt the General we will lift our ſwords<br>And either lanch his greedie thirſting throat,<br>Or take him priſoner, and his chaine ſhall ſerue<br>For Manackles, till he be '''ranſom’d''' home.}}
# To [[exact]] a ransom (payment) in exchange for the freedom of.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2017|author=Bruce Oliver Newsome; James W. Stewart; Aarefah Mosavi|title=Countering New(est) Terrorism: Hostage-Taking, Kidnapping, and Active Violence — Assessing, Negotiating, and Assaulting|publisher=CRC Press|isbn=9781351385701
|passage=Terrorists will continue to hold few detainees in undisclosed locations in order to '''ransom''' them for money or some other material profit, {{...}}}}

